\begin{aligned}&(5p+1)-2p\cdot4\\ =&5p+1-8p\\ =&-3p+1\end{aligned}
Now let's we simplify the outer pair of brackets:
\begin{aligned}&(-3p+1)(3)+(4-1\div3)(6p-9)\\ =&-9p+3+\frac{108}{3}p-\frac{108}{3}\\ =&-9p+3+36p-36\\ =&27p-33\end{aligned}
The final simplified expression is of the form $ap-b$, where $a$ is the coefficient of $p$, $b$ is the constant term. In this case, $a=27$ and $b=33$. Therefore, the answer is $27p-33$.

